ookbook:Slicing|sliced]] [[Cookbook:Mushroom|mushrooms]]\n* 1 cup [[Cookbook:Bulgur|bulgur]] or cracked wheat\n* ¼ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] dried [[Cookbook:Dill|dillweed]]\n* ¼ tsp dried whole [[Cookbook:Oregano|oregano]]\n* ½ tsp [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* ¼ tsp [[Cookbook:Pepper|pepper]]\n* 2 cups chicken or vegetable [[Cookbook:Broth|broth]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n# Melt margarine in a large [[Cookbook:Frying Pan|skillet]]; add celery, onion and mushrooms. Stir until vegetables are tender.\n# Add bulgur and cook until golden.\n# Add seasonings and broth. Cover and bring to a [[Cookbook:Boiling|boil]].\n# Reduce heat and [[Cookbook:Simmering|simmer]] for 15 minutes.\n# Serve.\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n\n* If you are cooking on a gas stove, make sure to stir once or twice during the 15 minute simmering.\n* If available, try sprinkling in a little fresh [[Cookbook:Parsley|parsley]] at the end of the cook time.\n\n[[Category:Boiled recipes]]\n[[Category:Side dish recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using bulgur]]\n[[Category:Recipes using celery]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chicken broth and stock]]\n[[Category:Recipes using vegetable broth and stock]]\n[[Category:Recipes using margarine]]\n[[Category:Recipes using mushroom]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Garden Bulgur","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"2 Tbsp margarine","sourceText":"2 Tbsp margarine","amountText":"2 Tbsp margarine","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"½ cup chopped celery","sourceText":"½ cup chopped celery","amountText":"½ cup chopped celery","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"1 medium onion, chopped (or a little less)","sourceText":"1 medium onion, chopped (or a little less)","amountText":"1 medium onion, chopped (or a little less)","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"1 cup fresh sliced mushrooms","source